solution.p:
The opposite action to multiplying by a fraction is multiplying by its reciprocal. When we multiply by a negative number, the inequality sign must change direction.
\begin{gathered}
{-{\frac{9}{4}}h}\lt{-{\frac{27}{4}}}\\
\multiplyleft{{-{\frac{4}{9}}}}{-{\frac{9}{4}}h}\secondhighlight{\gt}\multiplyleft{{-{\frac{4}{9}}}}{-{\frac{27}{4}}}\\
h \gt 3
\end{gathered}
So in set-builder notation, the solution set is {\{ h \mid h > 3 \}}\text{.}

